# Non-Immersive HUD Indicator SVG Conversion

Scope: Convert the 24 remaining non-immersive indicator PNGs to SVG, then ensure all non-immersive SVG indicator icons render at their final on-screen pixel size without texture rescaling.
Asset paths below are relative to VanillaExpanded/assets/vanillaexpanded/textures/hud/.
Immersive and legacy gauge artwork are excluded. Existing SVG artwork, including weather composite layers, requires no conversion but is included in the final rendering phase.

Phases 1-6 each target one indicator and include its asset conversions, loader updates, PNG removal, and verification.
Conversion phases are independent; their numbering provides a suggested execution order. Phase 7 follows completion of all conversion phases.
All in-game verification is deferred until the end of Phase 7, after all implementation and automated verification. It does not block completion of earlier phases.

## Completion criteria for every conversion task
    - Create a genuine vector SVG beside the PNG with the same base name; do not embed raster artwork.
    - Preserve the icon's meaning, transparent canvas, proportions, alignment, and layering behavior.
    - Preserve runtime tinting and fill/clipping behavior where applicable.
    - Update all relevant loading paths, pack checks, and test expectations to use the SVG.
    - For paths shared by multiple icons, switch only when every asset selectable through that path is ready.
    - Verify SVG loading, texture ownership, replacement, caching, and disposal through the existing rendering path.
    - Remove the PNG only after no runtime path or asset requirement depends on it.
    - Update directly affected documentation and tests; run focused regression tests.
    - Defer in-game appearance and state-transition checks to the final verification task in Phase 7.

## Phase 1: Approximate time - Icon style (7 tasks)
    Keep the immersive clock artwork and behavior unchanged. Complete all seven SVGs before switching the shared period-based loading path.
    [x] Convert approximate-time/unknown.png to unknown.svg, preserving the unknown-time state.
    [x] Convert approximate-time/dawn.png to dawn.svg, preserving the dawn state.
    [x] Convert approximate-time/morning.png to morning.svg, preserving the morning state.
    [x] Convert approximate-time/noon.png to noon.svg, preserving the noon state.
    [x] Convert approximate-time/afternoon.png to afternoon.svg, preserving the afternoon state.
    [x] Convert approximate-time/dusk.png to dusk.svg, preserving the dusk state.
    [x] Convert approximate-time/night.png to night.svg, preserving the night state.

## Phase 2: Body temperature (4 tasks)
    Keep the fill and outline canvases aligned. Complete both chevron SVGs before switching their shared direction-based loading path.
    [x] Convert body-temperature/fill-mask.png to fill-mask.svg, preserving runtime risk tinting and the clipped fill reveal.
    [x] Convert body-temperature/outline.png to outline.svg, preserving alignment with the fill mask.
    [x] Convert body-temperature/chevron-up.png to chevron-up.svg, preserving upward trend direction, tinting, and repeated-marker layout.
    [x] Convert body-temperature/chevron-down.png to chevron-down.svg, preserving downward trend direction, tinting, and repeated-marker layout.

## Phase 3: Player wetness (2 tasks)
    Complete both SVGs before switching the shared fill/outline loading path; preserve both drop instances.
    [x] Convert player-wetness/fill-mask.png to fill-mask.svg, preserving runtime tinting and alignment with each drop outline.
    [x] Convert player-wetness/outline.png to outline.svg, preserving alignment with the fill mask at both drop sizes.

## Phase 4: Rift activity (4 tasks)
    Preserve distinguishable activity levels and the accompanying reading. Complete all four SVGs before switching the shared level-based loading path.
    [x] Convert rift-activity/low.png to low.svg.
    [x] Convert rift-activity/medium.png to medium.svg.
    [x] Convert rift-activity/high.png to high.svg.
    [x] Convert rift-activity/apocalyptic.png to apocalyptic.svg.

## Phase 5: Temporal storm (3 tasks)
    Preserve distinguishable stages and existing pulse/visibility behavior. Complete all three SVGs before switching the shared stage-based loading path.
    [x] Convert temporal-storm/approaching.png to approaching.svg.
    [x] Convert temporal-storm/imminent.png to imminent.svg.
    [x] Convert temporal-storm/active.png to active.svg.

## Phase 6: Weather fallback icons (4 tasks)
    Preserve fallback selection when the composite SVG pack is absent or incomplete, including the split precipitation/fog layout.
    Complete rain, snow, and hail SVGs before switching the shared precipitation loading path. Keep fallback icons independent of composite-pack availability.
    [x] Convert weather/rain.png to rain.svg.
    [x] Convert weather/snow.png to snow.svg.
    [x] Convert weather/hail.png to hail.svg.
    [x] Convert weather/fog.png to fog.svg.

## Phase 7: Native-pixel SVG rendering for all non-immersive indicators
    Prerequisite: Complete phases 1-6.
    Include converted icons and existing calendar-date, environmental-temperature, wind-speed, shelter, and weather composite SVG icons.
    Native pixel size means the dimensions of the rasterized SVG texture, not the SVG's authored canvas dimensions.
    [ ] Derive each icon instance's final on-screen width and height in physical pixels from resolved layout, indicator size settings, GUI scale, and any additional applicable display scaling.
    [ ] Define consistent pixel rounding and placement so raster dimensions and destination dimensions agree exactly, including fractional GUI scales.
    [ ] Rasterize each SVG directly at those final pixel dimensions, preserving its aspect ratio and transparent canvas; remove fixed-size rasterization followed by texture enlargement or reduction.
    [ ] Draw every rasterized icon at exactly its texture's native pixel width and height (1:1 texel-to-screen-pixel mapping); never rescale the rasterized icon during drawing.
    [ ] Recompute required raster dimensions after layout, size-setting, GUI-scale, or display-scale changes and replace the texture before drawing at the new size; never stretch an old texture while waiting.
    [ ] Make texture reuse size-aware so differently sized instances cannot reuse an incorrectly sized raster; avoid rasterizing again when asset identity and required dimensions are unchanged.
    [ ] Apply the same sizing contract to layered masks, outlines, chevrons, both wetness drops, and full-size or split weather layers; clipping must reveal artwork without rescaling its full raster.
    [ ] Preserve visibility transitions, tinting, pulse effects, clipping, and alignment without scaling rasterized icons; keep rasterization and resource replacement outside per-frame drawing.
    [ ] Preserve generated-texture ownership and dispose replaced or retired textures without disrupting other live compositions.
    [ ] Add focused regression tests verifying requested SVG raster dimensions equal final draw dimensions, size changes trigger correctly sized replacements, unchanged sizes reuse textures, and replacement/teardown release owned resources.
    [ ] Update affected rendering documentation to describe final-size rasterization and native-pixel drawing.
    [ ] As the final verification step after all implementation and automated checks, verify all affected indicators in-game at supported indicator sizes and GUI scales, including fractional scales, live size changes, layered icons, split weather fallback layouts, and relevant state/style transitions.
    Completion: Every non-immersive SVG icon is rasterized for its actual destination size and drawn 1:1, with no upscaling or downscaling of the resulting texture.
